    fix(commander): clamp num_events from arming_check_reply (#28598)
    
    num_events is a uint8 while events is a fixed array of five, and the reply
    arrives on /fmu/in/arming_check_reply, which uXRCE-DDS exposes as an input
    topic. checkAndReport() looped to num_events and memcpy'd into events[i], so a
    value above five wrote past the end of the heap-allocated reply.
    
    Clamp on ingestion, next to the existing registration_id validation, so the
    stored reply cannot describe more events than it can hold.
    
    Reported by @REYu6.
    
    Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5[1m]
    
    Signed-off-by: Julian Oes <julian@oes.ch>

diff --git a/src/modules/commander/HealthAndArmingChecks/checks/externalChecks.cpp b/src/modules/commander/HealthAndArmingChecks/checks/externalChecks.cpp
index 93bcfce7df..8b9843c9fe 100644
--- a/src/modules/commander/HealthAndArmingChecks/checks/externalChecks.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/commander/HealthAndArmingChecks/checks/externalChecks.cpp
@@ -260,6 +260,15 @@ void ExternalChecks::update()
 			}
 
 			if (_registrations[reply.registration_id].reply) {
+				// num_events is a uint8 arriving on an externally writable topic, while events is
+				// a fixed-size array. Clamp it here, next to the registration_id check, so
+				// checkAndReport() cannot iterate past the end of the array.
+				static constexpr uint8_t max_num_events = sizeof(reply.events) / sizeof(reply.events[0]);
+
+				if (reply.num_events > max_num_events) {
+					reply.num_events = max_num_events;
+				}
+
 				*_registrations[reply.registration_id].reply = reply;
 			}
 
